# Review: DiagramStack

The code meets this spec closely. The scene and semantic types match field for field, the three
diagram kinds are dispatched in both `Dsl.parse` and `Dsl.compile`, and `checkKind` in
`dsl/parse.ts` turns sequence-only and data-flow-only words into errors and ignored hints into
warnings. The sequence engine implements activations, nesting, fragment-bounded bars, return checks,
notes, fragments, label-driven spacing and stick-figure actors, and the data-flow rules emit the
four warnings the spec names. Mermaid is marked deprecated in the core compilers, in the `Generate`
operation and in the skills, and all four acceptance scenarios run as tests.

The gaps are in test depth, not behaviour. Nested activation offsets (F-2.4), the end of an
unreturned bar (F-2.5), the innermost-caller warning (F-2.6), stick-figure drawing (F-2.11),
data-flow hints (F-3.2) and parse/compile equivalence (F-1.4) have code but no assertion. One small
divergence: `checkKind` reports only the first ignored hint on an edge (waypoint, else side, else
relationship word), not each one.

Of 42 items: 36 done, 6 untested, 0 partial, 0 diverged, 0 missing.

